## Fun binary terms:  

Binary numbers have some fun names.  
As stated earlier, a single binary digit is called a bit.  
Each hex value is 4 bits and we call that a nibble.  
In other words, every 4 bits or every single hex value represents a "nibble" worth of data.  
8 bits is called a byte.  
Or to put it in other words, two nibbles make a byte.  
Who says programmers don't have a sense of humor?  

